  <running_head>Physicarum Lib. VI.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>I 3</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">&amp; dependentes, nempe spiritus influens</l>
    <l n="2">&amp; sanguis. Quæ omnia abstractione</l>
    <l n="3">quadam notionum &amp; commodiorum</l>
    <l n="4">nominum substitutione, ubi opus</l>
    <l n="5">est, possunt omni viventi applicari. Hoc</l>
    <l n="6">senfu etiam nunc calidum innatum &amp;</l>
    <l n="7">humidum radicale à corpore sejunxi, ut</l>
    <l n="8">nempe discentes ad Medicorum præce-</l>
    <l n="9">ptiones &amp; dogmata magis aptarem.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">§. 2. Sed quærat quisquam : <i>qui re-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>lius rem expediant</i>, <i>Philosophi an Medi-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>ci</i>? Etsi maxima de nomine lis est :</l>
    <l n="13">tamen Philosophi videntur hanc rem ex-</l>
    <l n="14">pedire accuratius. Nam calidum</l>
    <l n="15">innatum, &amp; humidum radicale non existit</l>
    <l n="16">in corpore tanquam aliquid ab eo se-</l>
    <l n="17">junctum, sed quasi quicquam ad essen-</l>
    <l n="18">tiam ejus pertinens, quatenus nempe</l>
    <l n="19">corpus ut materia viventis accipitur.</l>
    <l n="20">Attamen cum Medicis loqui licebit,</l>
    <l n="21">hoc observato : quod materia viven-</l>
    <l n="22">tium adæquata mistum secundum sit,</l>
    <l n="23">cujus singulæ partes, sed diversa pro-</l>
    <l n="24">portione, &amp; essentia quandoque con-</l>
    <l n="25">stant aliquo, quod terræ respondeat, &amp;</l>
    <l n="26">Medici corpus appellent : aliquo quod</l>
    <l n="27">aquæ vices subeat, Medicisque humi-</l>
    <l n="28">dum radicale vocetur : &amp; aliquo quod</l>
    <l n="29">ignis rationem subeat ; &amp; à Medicis</l>
    <l n="30">calidum innatum nominetur.</l>
    <l n="31" type="foot" para="true">XX.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed number "I 3" at foot is a gathering signature; "XX." is a catchword-like mark at the foot right. Some words in the scan are uncertain due to the faded print (e.g. "relius", "Etsi"), transcribed as printed.</notes>
